# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill it in. `.env` is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Vite loads this file for both `pnpm dev` and `pnpm build`. Only variables
# prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser; everything else stays on the
# server. On Vercel, set these under Settings → Environment Variables instead.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Support email delivery (SMTP, via Brevo) ──────────────────────────────────
# Support form submissions are emailed to you over SMTP. Set these and every
# message users send from /support lands in your inbox; replying goes straight
# back to them (their address is set as Reply-To).
#
# This project uses Brevo (https://www.brevo.com). To get your credentials:
#   1. Log in to Brevo → https://app.brevo.com
#   2. Open "SMTP & API settings" → the "SMTP" tab
#   3. Copy your SMTP login (an email) and generate an SMTP key.
#      IMPORTANT: use an SMTP key, NOT an API key.
#   4. Verify your sender domain/address under Senders so SMTP_FROM is allowed.
#
# SMTP_HOST   Brevo's relay host. Always smtp-relay.brevo.com.
# SMTP_PORT   587 (STARTTLS, recommended) or 2525; or 465 for SSL/TLS.
# SMTP_USER   Your Brevo SMTP login (shown on the SMTP tab; an email address).
# SMTP_PASS   Your Brevo SMTP key (the generated key, not your account password).
# SMTP_FROM   The From address. Must be a verified sender in Brevo.
#             e.g. no-reply@gofullpageplus.com
# SUPPORT_TO  Where tickets are delivered. Your own inbox.
#             e.g. support@gofullpageplus.com
#
# Example:
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USER=your-login@smtp-brevo.com
#   SMTP_PASS=your-brevo-smtp-key
#   SMTP_FROM=no-reply@gofullpageplus.com
#   SUPPORT_TO=support@gofullpageplus.com
SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM=
SUPPORT_TO=

# ── Optional: server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port for `pnpm start` in production. Defaults to 3000.
# PORT=3000

# ── Optional: privacy-friendly analytics ─────────────────────────────────────
# Consumed by client/index.html. Leave both blank to ship no analytics at all,
# which is the simplest position to defend in a privacy policy.
VITE_ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT=
VITE_ANALYTICS_WEBSITE_ID=
